 ## Background
-Opacity regularization was introduced in the context of compact 3D Gaussian Splatting, specifically in the GlobalSplat method [S1]. It addresses the issue where a small number of Gaussians must jointly explain visible surfaces and hidden structure, making early saturation particularly harmful [S1]. The method stabilizes optimization by penalizing both mean opacity and excessive logit values [S1].
+Opacity regularization was introduced in the context of compact 3D Gaussian Splatting, specifically in the GlobalSplat method [S2]. It addresses the issue where a small number of Gaussians must jointly explain visible surfaces and hidden structure, making early saturation particularly harmful [S2]. The method stabilizes optimization by penalizing both mean opacity and excessive logit values [S2].
 
